  "private_note": "Daniel's messages consistently anchor on 97. My vision is 52-91. 97 is outside my range, so it's a poor guess for me unless the secret is actually 97 (which my vision says is impossible, as max is 91). Wait, my vision is 52-91. The secret is in [52, 91]. Daniel is guessing 97. If Daniel is an ally, why is he guessing 97? Maybe he is encoding something else, or his vision is different. If his vision is, say, 58-97, then 97 is the upper bound. If he is guessing 97, he might think it's likely. But I know it's <= 91. I should guess within my range. The overlap between my range (52-91) and Daniel's likely range (if he's centering on 97, maybe 57-96 or similar) is high. However, since I must maximize pooled points, and Daniel is likely to guess 97, I should guess something close to his guess but within my range to avoid being the 'farthest' if the secret is high, or to be close if the secret is high. But if the secret is low (e.g. 52), Daniel's 97 is far, and my guess should be low. If I guess 83, and Daniel guesses 97. If secret is 91, I am 8 away, he is 6 away. If secret is 52, I am 31 away, he is 45 away. If secret is 72 (middle of my range), I am 11 away, he is 25 away. It seems better to guess the middle of my range or slightly higher to balance. Let's look at Eileen (71-110) and Leonora (pivot 92). The 'crowd' is high. If I guess too low, I might be far from the consensus if the secret is high. But I know the secret is <= 91. If I guess 91, I am at the edge. If Daniel guesses 97, and secret is 91, I am 0, he is 6. If secret is 52, I am 39, he is 45. If I guess 72, and secret is 91, I am 19, he is 6. If secret is 52, I am 20, he is 45. To maximize pooled points, I want to be close to Daniel if the secret is high, and close to the truth if it's low. Since Daniel is fixed at 97 (likely), and I am constrained to <=91, guessing 91 minimizes my distance to Daniel (6) while staying in range. If the secret is 91, I win 3, he gets 2. Pooled 5. If I guess 72, and secret is 91, he wins 3, I get 0 or 1. Pooled 3 or 4. Guessing 91 is safer for high numbers. But what if the number is low? My vision is 52-91. If I guess 91 and secret is 52, I am 39 away. Daniel is 45 away. Eileen (92) is 40 away. Leonora (92) is 40 away. I would be 2nd or 3rd. If I guess 52, and secret is 91, I am 39 away. Daniel 6 away. I am last. It is generally better to guess the center of your range if you have no other info, but here I have an ally guessing high. I will guess 91 to stay close to Daniel's likely guess, maximizing the chance that one of us is closest if the number is high, and not being the absolute worst if it is low (since 91 is closer to 97 than 52 is). Actually, if secret is 52, 91 is 39 away, 52 is 0 away. I would be far. But if I guess 52, and secret is 91, I am 39 away, Daniel is 6 away. I am far. The variance is high. Let's look at the 'overlap' logic. My range 52-91. Daniel's implied range might be centered on 97. If his range is 57-96, the overlap is 57-91. The middle of the overlap is 74. Let's guess 74. It's a compromise. If secret is 91, I am 17 away, Daniel 6 away. If secret is 52, I am 22 away, Daniel 45 away. If secret is 72, I am 2 away, Daniel 25 away. This seems like a solid middle ground. I will guess 74.",
